In news:<1123080523.046476.297590@g47g2000cwa.googlegroups.com>,  
<dogscoff@eudoramail.com> says...
> My orc wizard just ate a goblin and got the "you feel evil and
> fiendish." I thought cannibalism was penalty-free for orcs, or does
> this message not do anything..?

That is meant as a *positive* message for a cannibalistic character. ;)

However it seems you get a -1 alignment hit (if not Cave[wo]man, they 
get a +1 alignment adjustment).
Nothing to care about really, compared to the heavy luck hit for others.





* spoily source code below *





---
	if (your_race(&mons[pm])) {
	    if (!CANNIBAL_ALLOWED()) {
		if (allowmsg) {
		    if (Upolyd)
			You("have a bad feeling deep inside.");
		    You("cannibal!  You will regret this!");
		}
		HAggravate_monster |= FROMOUTSIDE;
		change_luck(-rn1(4,2));		/* -5..-2 */
	    } else if (Role_if(PM_CAVEMAN)) {
		adjalign(sgn(u.ualign.type));
		You("honour the dead.");
	    } else {
		adjalign(-sgn(u.ualign.type));
		You_feel("evil and fiendish!");
	    }
	    return TRUE;
	}
